    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>Picture this: you're browsing an online perfume shop at 10pm. You click on a fragrance that sounds intriguing. The product description lists bergamot, pink pepper, saffron, Turkish rose, oud, and ambergris. It sounds magnificent, but what does that actually mean for what you will smell like when you put your jacket on tomorrow morning?</p><p>A fine fragrance is not a single, static scent. It is a living, evolving composition that unfolds over hours in three distinct movements. In perfumery, this structure is known as the Olfactory Pyramid.</p>"
      }
    },
