    "blogtextliquid_ra7Awx": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>The fragrance pyramid is dictated by the physical molecular weight of the ingredients. Lighter molecules evaporate into the air almost instantly, while heavy resinous molecules cling to skin for half a day.</p><p>Understanding how top, heart, and base notes interact is the single best tool you can have as a fragrance shopper. It prevents you from being misled by a 2-minute opening spray and guarantees you choose scents that evolve beautifully on your skin.</p>"
      }
    },
    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_614820f",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Top Notes: The 15-Minute Hook vs Heart Notes: The True Identity",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_size_mobile": 28,
            "heading_line_height": 1.1,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 30,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 25,
            "column_1_text": "<p>Top notes are the first impression. Made of light, volatile molecules like citrus (bergamot, lemon, grapefruit), fresh herbs, and light fruits, they hit your nose the instant you spray.</p><p>Their purpose is to captivate you immediately. However, they evaporate within 15 to 30 minutes. Never buy a perfume based purely on the opening spray—it is only the trailer, not the whole film.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>Heart notes (also called middle notes) emerge as the top notes fade. Composed of richer florals (jasmine, rose, lavender), spices (cardamom, cinnamon), and aromatics, heart notes represent the core personality of the fragrance.</p><p>They last anywhere from 2 to 5 hours, creating the radiant scent trail that people around you notice throughout the day.</p>",
            "body_size": 17,
            "body_size_mobile": 15,
            "body_line_height": 1.9,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 55,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_fb81b45",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "section_padding": 60,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "heading": "<p>Base notes: what you are actually wearing all day</p>",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_spacing": 25,
            "box_color": "#1C1917",
            "box_radius": 15,
            "box_padding": 45,
            "box_spacing": 35,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>Base notes are the heavy anchors of perfumery: sandalwood, cedarwood, patchouli, amber, vanilla, and musks. These molecules are large and dense, evaporating very slowly over 6 to 12+ hours.</p><p>The base notes provide the fixative foundation for the entire composition. When you catch a wonderful whiff of your own jumper or coat eight hours later, you are experiencing the base notes at work.</p><p>In masterfully blended perfumes like <strong>Addiction</strong> and <strong>Fierce</strong>, the transition from floral spice into warm amberwood is completely seamless.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#F5EFE6",
            "box_text_size": 17,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.9,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "subheading": "<p>Why this changes how you shop online</p>",
            "subheading_size": 42,
            "subheading_color": "#1A1816",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>When reading perfume note listings online, always scan down to the base notes first. If you dislike vanilla, patchouli, or heavy incense, a perfume with sweet or resinous base notes will eventually disappoint you, no matter how much you loved the fresh citrus opening.</p><p>Shop with the full 8-hour lifecycle in mind!</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 17,
            "bottom_text_color": "#2D2A26",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.9
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
